      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: We'll hear argument now in the Merck KGaA v. Integra Lifesciences."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1237",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "08cc65ab8c664abd9c2b74cef511fb498b771cfd862120fd21e5c65301244927",
      "evidence_id": "ev-08cc65ab8c66-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE O'CONNOR: Well, would you just clarify something for me as we start to consider the case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Merck KGaA",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1237",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "08cc65ab8c664abd9c2b74cef511fb498b771cfd862120fd21e5c65301244927",
      "evidence_id": "ev-08cc65ab8c66-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ROSENKRANZ: Thank you, Your -- Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Your Honors, there is no dispute among the parties, nor among the 19 amicus briefs presented before the Court today."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1237",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "08cc65ab8c664abd9c2b74cef511fb498b771cfd862120fd21e5c65301244927",
      "evidence_id": "ev-08cc65ab8c66-0000-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. JOSEFFER: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: I believe the question before the Court is the proper construction of the statute, and we believe the lower courts committed three important legal errors that should be corrected."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1237",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "08cc65ab8c664abd9c2b74cef511fb498b771cfd862120fd21e5c65301244927",
      "evidence_id": "ev-08cc65ab8c66-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But that might well determine whether the research was relatively directly related."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. JOSEFFER",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1237",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "08cc65ab8c664abd9c2b74cef511fb498b771cfd862120fd21e5c65301244927",
      "evidence_id": "ev-08cc65ab8c66-0001-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The first is that the Federal Circuit, as Justice O'Connor noted, reserved -- resolved these questions entirely as a matter of law, based on a de novo interpretation of the statute, without regard to the jury instruction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1237",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "08cc65ab8c664abd9c2b74cef511fb498b771cfd862120fd21e5c65301244927",
      "evidence_id": "ev-08cc65ab8c66-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What's your position on the jury instruction? Does it correctly state the law?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. JOSEFFER",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1237",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "08cc65ab8c664abd9c2b74cef511fb498b771cfd862120fd21e5c65301244927",
      "evidence_id": "ev-08cc65ab8c66-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yes. In fact, this Court already held in Eli Lilly v. Medtronic that the statute is not limited to generic drugs."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. JOSEFFER",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1237",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "08cc65ab8c664abd9c2b74cef511fb498b771cfd862120fd21e5c65301244927",
      "evidence_id": "ev-08cc65ab8c66-0001-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That's contrary to federal law. I -- certainly would be severe civil consequences. And my guess is there are criminal consequences for doing that, too."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1237",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "08cc65ab8c664abd9c2b74cef511fb498b771cfd862120fd21e5c65301244927",
      "evidence_id": "ev-08cc65ab8c66-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Did the earlier process that you described, the basic research, is that within the common law research exemption?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1237",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "08cc65ab8c664abd9c2b74cef511fb498b771cfd862120fd21e5c65301244927",
      "evidence_id": "ev-08cc65ab8c66-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, don't you think that the Federal Circuit may have focused too much on generic drug applications?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1237",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "08cc65ab8c664abd9c2b74cef511fb498b771cfd862120fd21e5c65301244927",
      "evidence_id": "ev-08cc65ab8c66-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE O'CONNOR: Can you repeat that 355 what?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1237",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "08cc65ab8c664abd9c2b74cef511fb498b771cfd862120fd21e5c65301244927",
      "evidence_id": "ev-08cc65ab8c66-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Is this text that you're referring to, is it someplace -- is the text someplace where we can look at it while you're explaining this to us?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1237",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "08cc65ab8c664abd9c2b74cef511fb498b771cfd862120fd21e5c65301244927",
      "evidence_id": "ev-08cc65ab8c66-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: What are you reading from?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1237",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "08cc65ab8c664abd9c2b74cef511fb498b771cfd862120fd21e5c65301244927",
      "evidence_id": "ev-08cc65ab8c66-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: In fact, that paragraph refers to effectiveness, as I read it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1237",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "08cc65ab8c664abd9c2b74cef511fb498b771cfd862120fd21e5c65301244927",
      "evidence_id": "ev-08cc65ab8c66-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: I don't -- so what? I don't understand what conclusion that leads to."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1237",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "08cc65ab8c664abd9c2b74cef511fb498b771cfd862120fd21e5c65301244927",
      "evidence_id": "ev-08cc65ab8c66-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ROSENKRANZ: Thank you, Your Honor. With my two minutes, I want to make one overarching important point, and it's really in response to a question Justice Scalia asked."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
